-- title:
--   Integrality over A[1/j] forces Laurent coefficients into A
-- statement:
--   Fix a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a nonzero natural number $M$. Let $F_M \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ be the subfield generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ \mathrm{jq}$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M$, and let $\mathcal{L}$ be the subfield `laurentBaseChange` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of $F_M$ under the map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $e \in \mathcal{L}$, and let $R =$ `affineBaseInf M A` be the subring of $\mathcal{L}$ generated by the constants $\{a : a \in A\} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \mathcal{L}$ together with the single element $(\bar{j})^{-1}$, where $\bar{j}$ is the coefficientwise image in $\mathcal{L}$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Assume $e$ is integral over $R$, i.e. there is a monic polynomial $p$ with coefficients in $R$ with $p(e) = 0$ in $\mathcal{L}$. The conclusion is that $e$, regarded as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, lies in `integralCoeffs A.toSubring`: each coefficient $e_n$, $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, belongs to $A$.
--
--   This is the integral-closedness statement for the pole chart of the modular curve over a valuation ring: the subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ is integrally closed in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, and $A[1/j]$ lies inside it. It is used in the construction of the characteristic-$p$ fibre model, in particular in the computations of the specialised places on the cuspidal chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_mem_integralCoeffs_of_integral_affineBaseInf.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_FibreModel
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_CharPReduction

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open AlgebraicCurve ModularCurve.CharPModel ModularCurve.CharPReduction in

theorem ModularCurve.mem_integralCoeffs_of_integral_affineBaseInf
    (A : ValuationSubring (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)) (M : ℕ) [NeZero M]
    (e : laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull M))
    (he : ∃ p : Polynomial (affineBaseInf M A), p.Monic ∧
      Polynomial.eval₂ (affineBaseInf M A).subtype e p = 0) :
    (e : LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)) ∈ integralCoeffs A.toSubring := by sorry
